// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P926136978" "Baron Zukor, huh? I haven't heard of him, but that doesn't necessarily mean he's small-time. My operations are mostly confined to Cap.<br><br>I'm intrigued by your interactions with the other Destined Ones, {HeroName}. Direct mind control is almost a form of puppetry, but it sounds to me like Zukor's followers retain their basic personalities, even after meeting with him. What's more, your Psychic Damper was only active for about a minute, and then all psychic influence ceased.<br><br>I'm not aware of any psychic powers capable of that level of mind-control, {HeroName}. For him to be able to retain his followers' loyalty, without directly altering their minds or maintaining psychic pressure... well, he's either very good or he's using something other than mind-control."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - LongbowTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P4058440470" "Longbow appreciates your support in this operation, {HeroName}. We'll take over from here."
// Answer Text :
"P3884708633" "Wait, why is Longbow here?"
// Page WhyHere Text :
"P2662798018" "<color orange>The Longbow officer eyes you suspiciously.</color><br><br>This is first and foremost a Longbow operation, {Hero.gender=male son|miss}. We were under the impression that you'd turned a new leaf, and would be happy to support our efforts against Arachnos.<br><br><color orange>The officer tenses slightly, appearing wary of you.</color><br><br>Is... there going to be a problem?"
// Answer Text :
"P204449647" "Not at all, officer. I was just curious."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable Group - depends_on_Boss Var Name - HELPER_VILLAIN 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable Group - depends_on_Boss Var Name - VILLAIN_STATEMENT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P2992779883" "{HeroName}, you're here! It's time to melt some faces!"
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P3271309201" "So we're the good guys, huh... never thought I'd see the day."
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P3312627431" "GOD, it's so good to finally get to DO something!"
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P953822625" "Hmph! It figures I'd end up paired with one of the wannabes!"
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P983886608" "Hey, {HeroName}! ICE to see you! Get it?<t 3>...Please don't kill me."
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P1813311880" "Hey, {HeroName}. Guess we're working together on this one."
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P4282308320" "<t 3>Hey, {HeroName}... plutonium or ner-<t 3>Oh, oops. Zukor told me to stop asking people that."
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P3579010030" "I am honored to be working beside you, {HeroName}. Together, we shall exact justice upon fools."
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P158404582" "<t 3>Hey, {HeroName}! I guess we're partners for this one.<t 0>This will be fun!"
// Script Variable VILLAIN_STATEMENT :
"P208632739" "Ah, {HeroName}. My thanks for handling Mangle the way that you did.<t 4>I would have happily defeated him myself, but the thought of being anywhere near him makes me wish to vomit."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P450638703" "I'll have my agents go through your report, {HeroName}. Hopefully we'll be able to get some insight on how Zukor is controlling your peers.<br><br>For the time being, you're going to need to remain in Baron Zukor's good graces. You've made good strides toward that goal already, but you're going to need to keep up appearances.<br><br><color orange>Ruben hands you a folded sheet of paper.</color><br><br>Our agents intercepted this missive just recently. It's from Zukor's cult, and it's addressed to you. They want you to attack a local Arachnos facility."
// AcceptString :
"P2679633249" "Attack Arachnos? I would never..."
// SendOffString :
"P2329729136" "Save it, {HeroName}. There's no need to play dumb, I know how things work in the Isles.<br><br>In this case, we've deemed the operation necessary, to maintain your cover. I've reviewed the personnel roster at the target's location and made a few minor changes - nothing conspicuous, I assure you. I just hate to waste competency. The standing force that remains... well, they would not represent a significant loss to Arachnos's presence in Cap au Diable.<br><br>The missive indicates that you'll be paired with another of Zukor's cultists. Make sure you remain convincing, but see if you can discern Zukor's motives in all this. We still don't know what he's up to."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3249578225" "Cripple the Arachnos Base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P922706391" "Get going, {HeroName}. The last thing we need right now is Zukor getting suspicious."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P885025968" "<color deepskyblue>Part Two: Acceptable Losses</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3498269365" "This is the base Zukor wanted you to hit.<br><br>As far as 'heroic' jobs go, knocking Arachnos heads isn't so bad. If you're going to go along with this charade, you may as well cut loose."
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - OnEnterObjectiveComplete 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3316051345" "Talk to the Longbow Officer"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - TimedObjective 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_25HEALTH_DIALOG :
"P459086836" "Ugh... I'm spent, {HeroName}. I can still advise you, but I won't be much use in a fight anymore."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2723077874" "Alright, let's see... the Baron said that we should aim for their communications first, so they can't call for reinforcements."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2982857144" "Okay, that's done. Next, we're supposed to prevent them from masking the base from outside detection. You don't... happen to know how they do that, do you?"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3747098066" "Last one on the list: this base has some nasty external defenses. We need to shut them down. Don't ask me why - it's on the list."
// Script Variable OBJECT_DISPLAYNAME :
"P3042677356" "Communications Array"
// Script Variable Greeting :
"P3609192693" "{HeroName}, it's you."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1822421929" "THAT TINGLE TELLS YOU I'M WORKING!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P892451606" "I die!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Thing1Destroyed 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P4202230951" "Disable the Arachnos communications array"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable OBJECT_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1569681057" "Electromagnetic Damper"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Thing2Destroyed 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P2673861817" "Expose the Arachnos base to detection"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable OBJECT_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1901325751" "Automated Defense System"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Thing3Destroyed 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P976701661" "Bring down the base's automated defenses"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2616962251" "Lieutenant Davidson"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3024239412" "Fan out! Secure the exits, then sweep for any stragglers. Let's move, people!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P1738482053" "Nevermind"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2172165910" "You've managed to subdue the base's defenses... and discovered something interesting in the process."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2401073003" "<i>Longbow?!?</i><br><br>I'm aware of their incursions on Fort Darwin, but I didn't think they'd be bold enough to try to take Cap au Diable so soon.<br><br>This makes sense, {HeroName}. For one man to try and turn all of the Destined Ones as a solo operation... that's beyond foolish. It would be suicidal.  With Longbow's backing, however, this gambit starts to make sense.<br><br>If Baron Zukor has their support, <i>and</i> manages to corral enough Destined Ones, he'd have a potent enough army to march on Aeon City.<br><br>For the record, <i>this</i> is why we didn't use the brute force approach. If we play this right, we can cause their whole operation to backfire."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DatabaseTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P1204361241" "<color orange>It appears that one of the nearby Longbow has done you the favor of logging into this database for you. How considerate.</color><br><br><color skyblue><color yellow>MISSION DATABASE MAIN PAGE</color><br><br>PLEASE ENTER QUERY"
// Answer Text :
"P2648511943" "(Search for anything related to Baron Zukor)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P2697783653" "<color orange>A number of pages appear after the search completes. A few contain snippets and references to Zukor from years past - apparently he originates from Paragon City - but one page in particular catches your eye:</color><br><br><color skyblue><color yellow>MISSION ID #58329</color> - OPERATION DESTINY FOLLOWS<BR><BR><color yellow>CONTRACTED AGENT</color> - Baron Zukor<br><br><color yellow>ASSETS PROVIDED</color> - Suggestion Engine (PROTOTYPE); Squadron Epsilon-One-Nine (ROLE: SUPPORT/GUARD; PERIOD: 3 MONTHS)<br><br><color yellow>MISSION GOALS:</color><BR><BR><color yellow>1)</color> Disruption of Arachnos Destined One program (FILE #07531)<BR><BR><color yellow>2)</color> Temporary Acquisition of Destined One forces as future assets for MISSION ID #54797 - OPERATION CAP D'ANGE<br><br><color yellow>3)</color> Disruption of Arachnos defenses, in support of MISSION ID #54797 - OPERATION CAP D'ANGE"
// Answer Text :
"P3826070898" "(Search the term 'Cap d'Ange')"
// Answer Text :
"P2805946284" "(Search the term 'Suggestion Engine')"
// Page CapAnge1 Text :
"P1823692397" "<color orange>The first page in your search appears to describe Longbow's long-term plans to occupy Cap au Diable:</color><br><br><color skyblue><color yellow>MISSION ID #54797 - OPERATION CAP D'ANGE</color><BR><BR>PRIORITY: <color #FF66AA>FUSCHIA</color><BR><BR><color yellow>PHASE 1</color> - Disrupt Arachnos defenses and prepare forces for occupation<br><br><color yellow>PHASE 2</color> - Advance occupation force; Removal of key Arachnos defenses; Occupation of Aeon City<br><br><color yellow>PHASE 3</color> - Occupation reinforcement; Interface with local populace; Removal of all Arachnos defenses; Establish perimeter fortifications"
// Page Suggestion1 Text :
"P1374786211" "<color orange>The first page in your search appears to describe an interesting prototype mind-altering device:</color><br><br><color skyblue><color yellow>ASSET ID #57331 - SUGGESTION ENGINE (PROTOTYPE)</color><BR><BR><color yellow>FUNCTION:</color><br>Amplify and alter existing psychic emanations for the purpose of long-term, low-risk psychic coercion.<br><br><color yellow>METHOD:</color><br>The Suggestion Engine absorbs psychic energy from a trained psychic and emanates that energy in the form of a low-yield wave pulse. Rather than affecting the target mind directly, it amplifies directives given to the target, making them more likely to follow instructions or believe fabricated statements.<br><br><color yellow>LIMITATIONS:</color><br>While the Suggestion Engine's wave pulse can amplify the statements of any individual, it must be consistently recharged with psychic emanations in order to function properly. Furthermore, it must be calibrated to a specific individual psychic's wavelength, and cannot absorb emanations from any psychic it has not been previously calibrated for.<br><br><color yellow>CURRENT STATUS:</color><br>On loan to Baron Zukor (CONTRACTED AGENT) for the purposes of field testing; implemented as part of MISSION ID #58329 - OPERATION DESTINY FOLLOWS."
// Page CapAnge2 Text :
"P3213192070" "<color orange>The first page in your search appears to describe Longbow's long-term plans to occupy Cap au Diable:</color><br><br><color skyblue><color yellow>MISSION ID #54797 - OPERATION CAP D'ANGE</color><BR><BR>PRIORITY: <color #FF66AA>FUSCHIA</color><BR><BR><color yellow>PHASE 1</color> - Disrupt Arachnos defenses and prepare forces for occupation<br><br><color yellow>PHASE 2</color> - Advance occupation force; Removal of key Arachnos defenses; Occupation of Aeon City<br><br><color yellow>PHASE 3</color> - Occupation reinforcement; Interface with local populace; Removal of all Arachnos defenses; Establish perimiter fortifications"
// Answer Text :
"P2956739504" "(Download all relevant pages and log off)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2314485222" "Now that we know that Longbow's involved, we know what kind of budget is backing our friend Baron Zukor. I think an investigation is in order. We know the locations of some nearby Longbow outposts, but...<br><br><color orange>Ruben flips through a few pages in his notebook. After perusing the pages for a moment, he lets out an exasperated sigh.</color><br><br>The problem I have is that I'm a little low on personnel, lately. The base you hit was only one of many, {HeroName}. I've been getting intermittent reports of Destined One attacks all day. I simply don't have the resources to mount an incursion into a Longbow stronghold at the moment.<br><br>Now, we could have you go in there and investigate yourself, but that presents a whole slew of new problems."
// AcceptString :
"P2176963554" "Foremost being, how do I do that without blowing my cover?"
// SendOffString :
"P4118706980" "Exactly. My recommendation is that you assume the identity of an Arachnos agent. I'll see what I can scrounge up for you to wear.<br><br>This way, you'll have at least <i>some</i> freedom to investigate without immediately tipping your hand to Zukor.<br><br>Just... try to be discreet, if you can. They probably have an extensive file on you, and the disguise won't mask your powers. Get in, find whatever info you can, and get out."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2919405573" "Investigate Zukor's Connection with Longbow"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3878947888" "We need to do this fast, {HeroName}. There's no telling when you'll get another summons from Zukor."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3522428646" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Double Agent</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P796360809" "Longbow shouldn't see you as anything more than a simple Arachnos agent.<br><br>...Hopefully."
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P432048828" "Access the Longbow database"
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - OnEnterGrantPowerMission 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// - ScriptDef - SetObjectiveText 
// ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P221480987" "Fend off the Longbow security teams!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3571567476" "Now we die..."
// Script Variable PET_NAME :
"P361315832" "Longbow Database"
// Script Variable PET_DISPLAYINFO :
"P638507587" "This computer terminal grants access to Longbow's mission database. If they have any info on Baron Zukor, it will be here."
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P198285215" "<t 2><t 0>Zukor can be trusted. We just need to buy him enough time to succeed."
// Script Variable CAPTOR_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P2337896154" "Do you really think this is going to work?"
// Script Variable CAPTOR_ACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P269042253" "That's time we might not have! Look alive!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2409989984" "Now we fight"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4123400303" "Find the intruder! We cannot let our operations be compromised!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3951503766" "It's just one agent! Take {Hero.gender=male him|her} out, NOW!"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P4263017519" "There's something odd about this one... {Hero.gender=male he|she} doesn't move like a normal agent..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - FinalAmbushDefeated 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P690396897" "You infiltrated the Longbow base and learned about the Suggestion Engine."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P673016436" "Amazing find, {HeroName}. Thanks to the info you've gathered, we now have a clear picture of how Zukor is manipulating the Destined Ones.<br><br>To be honest, 'Operation Cap d'Ange' doesn't tell me anything new, other than the fact that Longbow is completely devoid of originality. We had already guessed what their plans were in Cap; it's essentially the same plan they implemented in Mercy Island.<br><br>This Suggestion Engine, though... it sounds like it's truly a remarkable device. It appears that it's currently calibrated to Zukor's psychic wavelength, so we're not going to be able to charge it ourselves. However, the schematics imply that once the Engine is charged, anyone can use it to 'persuade' their targets.<br><br>I think you know where I'm going with this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ZukorTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Friendly Text :
"P1462613476" "You look troubled, {HeroName}. Speak your mind."
// Answer Text :
"P4010983430" "Baron, I think we should speak privately. It's rather urgent."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P892684464" "<color orange>Zukor pauses to hear Pyra's entreaty, but soon cuts her off angrily.<br><br></color>Pyra, for the last time. I will not have you sowing doubt amongst my followers. I have spoken with each of you, and I am quite confident in the loyalty of everyone in this room.<br><br><color orange>Zukor turns to face you.</color><br><br>We can meet in private, {HeroName}, but this must be brief. We still have much to do."
// Answer Text :
"P2910850243" "I promise it will not take long."
// Page Confront Text :
"P2850527119" "Here we are, {HeroName}. Now, what is so important that it could not be heard by the rest of my council?"
// Answer Text :
"P3732946567" "I wanted to talk with you about the Suggestion Engine."
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P1474217102" "<color orange>The device in your ear immediately begins buzzing madly, almost painfully. Zukor is staring at you intently.</color><br><br>I'm sure I <b><i>don't know</b></i> what you're <b><i>talking about</b></i>, {HeroName}. How can you be <b><i>sure</b></i> that such a thing even <b><i>exists</b></i>?"
// Answer Text :
"P1232473482" "Oh, I'm sure. I'll be using it myself, soon enough."
// Answer Text :
"P531718221" "Does talking like that help 'convince' people, or is that just how you talk normally?"
// Page InformationPage4 Text :
"P3372096085" "<color orange>Zukor remains silent, gritting his teeth. After a moment, he speaks in a low, calm tone.</color><br><br>It is clear that my <i>suggestions</i> are not diverting you, for whatever reason. Perhaps a more direct approach will be more effective."
// Answer Text :
"P327774534" "I doubt it, but you're welcome to try."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - MartialGloomTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P2859260933" "What's going on? Where's the Baron?"
// Answer Text :
"P4085175689" "I'll explain soon, but I need to speak with everyone."
// Answer Text :
"P4152940697" "Back off, Gloom, or I'll make you wish you'd never been born."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P4166447412" "<color orange>Martial Gloom's brow furrows in suspicion, but he quickly relents. The Suggestion Engine must already be working on him.</color><br><br>Yes... yes I can see that you do. Please, by all means, {HeroName}. The podium is all yours."
// Answer Text :
"P4276794686" "Much appreciated."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P3848230354" "<color orange>Martial Gloom's eyes widen in fright, and he backs away from you slowly.</color><br><br>Please! Don't hurt me, I didn't mean to stop you! I won't do it again!<br><br><color orange>From his reaction, it is apparent that the Suggestion Engine works on threats as well.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1446409732" "Just get out of my way."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - PodiumTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P2155653646" "<color orange>As you approach the podium, your audience looks up at you, confused. The Suggestion Engine should be enough to convince these people to do what you wish, but you'll still have to give a speech in order for it to work.<br><br>You should probably begin with what's already on everyone's minds: Where is Baron Zukor?"
// Answer Text :
"P1168757310" "He's elsewhere, and he told me to take over."
// Answer Text :
"P3206681112" "Longbow assassinated him."
// Answer Text :
"P2837750833" "He betrayed us, so I killed him."
// Page Elsewhere Text :
"P1485675029" "<color orange>The podium projects your voice, causing it to reverberate off the walls of the room.<br><br>You tell your fellow Villains that Baron Zukor has chosen to move on to other lands, convincing Villains to change their ways and become champions of justice. You declare that he has asked me to take over the organization, and to lead his followers to great and glorious acts.<br><br>You also accuse Longbow of moving to intercept and capture him. You finish with an impassioned plea to your fellows to protect the Baron from Longbow's schemes.<br><br>Now would be a good time to talk about what to do next."
// Answer Text :
"P140385016" "I'll follow in the spirit of Zukor and make sure we do good works."
// Answer Text :
"P2959598527" "You're all villains, and you should wake up and start acting like it."
// Answer Text :
"P129365989" "You'll all follow my orders or I'll personally slay all of you."
// Page Assassinated Text :
"P3488403839" "<color orange>The podium projects your voice, causing it to reverberate off the walls of the room.<br><br>You warn your fellow Destined Ones that a great tragedy has befallen their cause. You tell them that Baron Zukor has been killed, by one of their own.<br><br>You accuse Pyra, one of the Baron's trusted lieutenants, of working as a spy for Longbow. You claim that, on their orders, she assassinated the Baron before you had a chance to stop her. You state that Pyra has been dealt with, but acknowledge that all of you suffer from the loss of your leader.<br><br>You state that, in honor of his memory and his deeds, you will lead them in the Baron's stead, and claim that it is what he would have wanted.<br><br>Now would be a good time to talk about what to do next."
// Page TakeCredit Text :
"P2194536849" "<color orange>The podium projects your voice, causing it to reverberate off the walls of the room.<br><br>You declare firmly to your de-facto brothers and sisters that you bring grave news: that you have all been betrayed. You explain to everyone that Baron Zukor, the one in whom they placed so much trust, had been plotting against all of them from the beginning.<br><br>You detail the deal he made with Longbow, and reveal the fact that he has been using psychic tricks to charm them all.<br><br>You state that Zukor cannot control them now, as you have taken care of him yourself. With a sweeping gesture, you declare that their minds are now their own.<br><br>Now would be a good time to talk about what to do next."
// Page StillGood Text :
"P1763645855" "<color orange>You remind your peers that they are capable of doing great and wonderful things, and that they are capable of changing the world for the better.<br><br>You declare that It is <b><i>Longbow</b></i> that has shown their true colors, as an enemy of all that is good and just. You state that if you are to follow in the spirit of justice, you cannot allow them to act in such a despicable manner.<br><br>It's about time to wrap this speech up. Time for your final statements."
// Answer Text :
"P3038921993" "Order an attack on the main Longbow base."
// Page BackToVillain Text :
"P3332820620" "<color orange>You declare to your fellow Destined Ones that, while you all have dabbled in heroism, deep down you all know that you are not Heroes. You remind them that they are in the Rogue Isles, where the only law is survival of the fittest. You point to the crowd, and cry that you all are the few who stand tall above the rest, who refuse to bow to <b><i>anyone</b></i>; not Arachnos, and not Longbow.<br><br>You shout that you have fought, tooth and nail, to achieve dominance over your enemies, and you will continue to fight. You declare that you will bring Longbow to their knees, and show them that no one - <b><i>no one</b></i> - messes with the Villains of the Rogue Isles.<br><br>It's about time to wrap this speech up. Time for your final statements."
// Page IronFist Text :
"P2043398614" "<color orange>You begin by asking the crowd if they hope for a leader like Zukor: one that acts with compassion, wisdom, and care. You then firmly warn them to dash those hopes now and forever. You remind them that you are not Baron Zukor, nor will you ever be.<br><br>You declare that when you give an order, it is a <b><i>command</b></i>, not a request. You warn that you will not sit idly and listen to them whine about their sorry excuses for lives. You order them all to <i><b>do as they are told</i></b>, or they will <b><i>die</b></i> by your hand.<br><br>It's about time to wrap this speech up. Time for your final statements."
// Page AttackBase Text :
"P531157614" "<color orange>You declare that now is the time to bring the fight to Longbow.<br><br>You relate how, soon, you will march upon their base, <b><i>slay</i></b> their commander, and <b><i>slaughter</b></i> their soldiers.<br><br>You instruct them that this will be a day long-remembered. You remind them that each of them has been wronged, and it is time for them to repay Longbow for what they have done.<br><br>You point down into the crowd, at Double Tap, and order him to rally your fighters and prepare for an assault on Longbow's headquarters. You then tell the crowd that you will join them shortly... at which point the assault will begin."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - RubenTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Start Text :
"P464316625" "I witnessed your speech through the Network, {HeroName}. Good work. You seem to have them all marching to your tune.<br><br>If we're going to stop Longbow in time, we're going to need to move quickly. I'll send Double Tap the coordinates for their main base, but you'll probably want to be present to direct the assault.<br><br>We still don't know much about the Suggestion Device, and we can't be sure that its effects will last long enough to keep the Destined Ones following your orders. At the very least, your presence there will make them more likely to remain a cohesive force."
// Answer Text :
"P483236664" "I wouldn't want to miss this, anyway."
// Answer Text :
"P3157203163" "And why, exactly, would I use MY army to fight Longbow?"
// Page Agreeable Text :
"P3014972650" "I'm glad to hear it, {HeroName}. You've got the advantage now.<br><br><color orange>Ruben chuckles softly to himself.</color><br><br>I don't think Longbow stands a chance."
// Answer Text :
"P4120912213" "I'd have to agree."
// Page Disagreeable Text :
"P2124743512" "I'm not disputing your control over the Destined Ones, {HeroName}. To be perfectly honest, I don't think I could even if I wanted to. The fact is, however, that Longbow has forced both of our hands.<br><br>As we speak, they're mobilizing a force to take control of Aeon City. That's bad for me, because it's bad for Arachnos. But they also have a file on all of Zukor's recruits, and you can bet they'll be gunning for every last one of you.<br><br>Now, you could just take your army and try to evacuate Cap, but even if that were to work, you've got the Suggestion Engine's limitations to worry about. Your army won't be loyal to you forever.<br><br>As it stands, there's really only one option left to you: take your army of Destined Ones - the only force in the area right now that's capable of contending with Longbow's forces - and destroy them before they destroy you."
// Answer Text :
"P1857871207" "That I can understand."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2587136992" "Now that we're aware of the Suggestion Engine, I think it's time we made our move. Zukor just recently sent out a summons to all of his cultists to return to the Meeting Grounds. I'm guessing he's getting ready to support Longbow in a major push towards Aeon City.<br><br>It's the perfect time to strike, {HeroName}. Zukor trusts you, thanks to your attack on our outpost, and you're going to need to capitalize on that trust.<br><br>See if you can get Zukor alone. If you attack him out in the open, you'll have the entire cult bearing down on you at once. If you can manage to get another private meeting, though..."
// AcceptString :
"P1756751245" "Trust me. I know EXACTLY what to do."
// SendOffString :
"P2172027697" "I'm glad we're on the same page, {HeroName}.<br><br>The Suggestion Engine is focused through a single projector, about the size of a pocketwatch. Zukor will probably be carrying it on him, as he'll want to have the Engine available if he needs to 'convince' anyone on the fly.<br><br>Once you've taken down Zukor, see if you can acquire that projector. That will let you influence the rest of the cultists - and that's when Longbow's plan blows up in their faces."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1772886251" "<color deepskyblue>Part Four: {Hero.gender=male Man|Woman} of the People</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound4_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

